  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Translation Projects now works by project. Each project row expands to show its items read-only, and Import, Publish and Refresh act on one whole project at a time; projects are named automatically as \"CMS Translations - [n] item(s)\", with no count repeated in the row. A project becomes ready for import only once every requested language has been delivered; until then it reads \"Partly delivered\" and names the languages it is waiting for, and the scheduled job does not import it. Publish is offered only once every language is imported and the content's master language is published in the CMS — the gadget says when that master-language publish is what is pending. Publishing a page publishes the nested blocks it depends on first, so a translated page no longer goes live over blocks still in draft. Once a project is imported, Publish is the only action left — Refresh is hidden, because every language is already in the CMS. A published project is final: no further actions are offered, and Refresh no longer walks a project back to an earlier status.",
